feat(api): accept Kinescope as an external video type

POST /api/v1/activities/external_video takes `type: "youtube" | "vimeo"`, so a
Kinescope video (kinescope.io) cannot be stored as an external video activity.
Kinescope is a widely used video host in Russia and the CIS.

Add "kinescope" to ExternalVideo.type. The activity keeps SUBTYPE_VIDEO_YOUTUBE,
which already covers Vimeo, and is told apart by content.type. Docs and the SDK
schema (packages/sdk, regenerated) follow.

Covered by `test_video_activity_service.py`: a Kinescope activity is created
with its uri and type; an unknown type is still rejected.
